(*"product_definition_schema.characterized_product"
A **characterized_product** is a type of <<express:product_property_definition_schema.characterized_object,characterized_object>> and a type of <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>> for the purpose of characterizing a product.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.characterized_product.__note"
Properties that are assigned using *characterized_object* are outside version control, whereas properties added via *product_definition* are under version control.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.source"
The **source** type is a list of alternate choices that enables one to characterize whether a product is to be manufactured within an organization, bought, or the fact that this information is not known.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.source.made"
characterize a product is to be manufactured within an organization;
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.source.bought"
characterize a product is to be bought;
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.source.not_known"
information, whether a product is to be manufactured within an organization or bought, is not known.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.alternative_solution_relationship"
An **alternative_solution_relationship** is a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation_relationship,product_definition_formation_relationship>> that specifies the type of the relationship.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.alternative_solution_relationship.relation_type"
the meaning of the relationship.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.alternative_solution_relationship.wr:WR1"
An **alternative_solution_relationship** shall not participate in its own definition.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product"
A **product** is a representation of a product or a type of product

A **product** depends on one or more instances of <<express:application_context_schema.product_context,product_context>> specifying a frame of reference that determines the validity of the information held about the product or class of products.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product.__example"
The SS Titanic is a product that could be represented by *product*.
*)
(*"product_definition_schema.product.__example"
Lifeboat is a class of products that could be represented by the entity data type *product*. Each lifeboat on the SS Titanic is a member of this class.
*)
(*"product_definition_schema.product.__example"
The computer used to edit this document, the Eiffel Tower, and coal are examples of products existing in the real world.
*)
(*"product_definition_schema.product.__example"
A company develops a new lawnmower, a product that will be realized through a manufacturing and assembly process.
*)
(*"product_definition_schema.product.__example"
Heating, lighting, and Internet connectivity are examples of functions.
*)
(*"product_definition_schema.product.__example"
A company may develop a generic engine that is described by a schematic drawing showing its main principles and components. This product may be used as the basis for a range of engines that share characteristics such as multi-valve and operating temperature. Then, when defining a new engine, designers create a specialization of this generic engine with specific characteristics such as cylinder volume and power.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product.__note"
The term product is defined in ISO 10303-1.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product.__note"
Products that this entity data type can represent include:



* products existing in the real world;
* products that may come into existence as a consequence of some realization process;
* products that are functions;
* products that require further detail so they may serve as the basis for other physically realizable products.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product.__note"
The products or classes of products that are represented by *product* are specified in annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity data type.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product.wr:IP1"
<<express:product_definition_schema.characterized_product,characterized_product>> shall be the only subtype of **product**.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **product**.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product.id.__example"
Part numbers, stock item numbers, and serial numbers are examples of product identifiers.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product.id.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product.id.__note"
The context in which id is used as a discriminating characteristic can be identified in an annotated Express schema that uses or specializes this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **product** is known.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product.name.__example"
'Widget' is an example of name.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **product**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product.frame_of_reference"
a set of <<express:application_context_schema.product_context,product_context>> entities that defines the contexts within which the data associated with the **product** is relevant.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_category"
A **product_category** is a classification that applies to products.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_category.__example"
In an application protocol whose context includes manufactured parts, 'mechanical part', 'electrical part', 'structural part', 'piping part', 'water pipe', and 'hot water pipe' are examples of types of product.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_category.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **product_category** is known.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_category.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **product_category**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_category.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **product_category**.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_category.id.__note"
This attribute is an upwardly compatible addition to *product_category* as specified in ISO 10303-41:1994.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_category.id.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_category.id.__note"
The context in which id is used as a discriminating characteristic can be identified in an annotated Express schema that uses or specializes this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_category.wr:WR1"
Each **product_category** shall be the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute.identified_item,identified_item>> in at most one <<express:basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute,id_attribute>>.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_category.wr:WR1.__note"
The <<express:basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute,id_attribute>> data type is defined in <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> of this document.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_category.wr:WR1.__note"
A template for constraining the population of the entity data types defined in the <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> is described in annex E.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_category.wr:IP1"
If a **product_category** participates in a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_category_relationship,product_category_relationship>> graph, the value of the name attribute shall not be identical to the name attribute within any of its parent **product_category** entity data types.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_category_relationship"
A **product_category_relationship** is a hierarchical relationship of one category with another and provides a description of their relationship. If a <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>> belongs to a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_category,product_category>>, it also belongs to all of the parent categories.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_category_relationship.__example"
The two sub-level <<express:product_definition_schema.product_category,product_category>>s called 'cold water pipe' and 'hot water pipe' can be related to each other through the more generic <<express:product_definition_schema.product_category,product_category>> called 'piping part' by using two *product_category_relationships*, one *product_category_relationship* between 'piping part' and 'cold water pipe' and the other *product_category_relationship* between 'piping part' and 'hot water pipe'.
*)
(*"product_definition_schema.product_category_relationship.__example"
A <<express:product_definition_schema.product_category,product_category>> called 'piping part' may be the parent category of sub-categories called 'cold water pipe' and 'hot water pipe'. The <<express:product_definition_schema.product_category,product_category>> called 'hot water pipe' may be a sub-category of another <<express:product_definition_schema.product_category,product_category>> called 'boiler output pipe'. This is an example of a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_category,product_category>> network because the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_category,product_category>> called 'hot water pipe' has two parents.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_category_relationship.__note"
The role of *product_category_relationship* can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_category_relationship.__note"
Networks of instances of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_category,product_category>> may be defined using this entity.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_category_relationship.__note"
This entity, in conjunction with the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_category,product_category>> entity, is based on the relationship template that is described in annex E.3.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_category_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **product_category_relationship** is known.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_category_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **product_category_relationship**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_category_relationship.category"
the parent of the **sub_category**.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_category_relationship.category.__example"
In the previous example, 'piping part' would be the category for 'cold water pipe' and 'hot water pipe'.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_category_relationship.sub_category"
a child of the **category**.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_category_relationship.sub_category.__example"
In the previous example 'cold water pipe' would be the *sub_category* for 'piping part' in one case and 'hot water pipe' would be the *sub_category* in the other.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_category_relationship.wr:WR1"
A graph of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_category,product_category>> instances shall not be cyclic.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition"
A **product_definition** is a representation of an aspect of a product, or of a class of products, for an identified life cycle stage. The life cycle stage for which a **product_definition** exists may be further characterized by discipline, by usage, or by both.

The **product_definition** entity data type may represent particular products that are the members of an identified class of products.

The **product_definition** entity data type acts as an aggregator for information about the properties of products.

The usage of a **product_definition** in another context is specified through its participation in a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship,product_definition_relationship>> as the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> in which the using context is specified by the **frame_of_reference** of the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>>.

If a **product_definition** is considered in multiple contexts, the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_context_association,product_definition_context_association>> shall be used to specify a collection of <<express:application_context_schema.product_definition_context,product_definition_context>>s.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition.__example"
The design of the SS Titanic and the as-built description of the SS Titanic can be represented as two instances of *product_definition* for the product that represents the ship itself.
*)
(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition.__example"
Each individual lifeboat on the SS Titanic can be represented by an instance of *product_definition*, in which the associated <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>> represents the class of products whose members are the lifeboats.
*)
(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition.__example"
The designed shape of an aeroplane can be identified by an instance of the <<express:product_property_definition_schema.product_definition_shape,product_definition_shape>> entity data type that is associated with the design *product_definition* of the aeroplane.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition.__note"
The *product_definition* entity type supports the representation of different views of a product for different purposes. Multiple views of the same product, or class of products, are represented by different instances of *product_definition* for the same <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation,product_definition_formation>>.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition.__note"
A *product_definition* can identify an occurrence of a product.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **product_definition**.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition.id.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition.id.__note"
The context in which id is used as a discriminating characteristic can be identified in an annotated Express schema that uses or specializes this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **product_definition**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition.formation"
the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation,product_definition_formation>> to which the **product_definition** relates.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition.frame_of_reference"
the <<express:application_context_schema.product_definition_context,product_definition_context>> in which the **product_definition** is defined.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **product_definition** is known.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition.name.__note"
This attribute is an upwardly compatible addition to *product_definition* as specified in ISO 10303-41:1994.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition.wr:WR1"
Each **product_definition** shall be the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute.named_item,named_item>> in at most one <<express:basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute,name_attribute>>.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition.wr:WR1.__note"
The <<express:basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute,name_attribute>> data type is defined in <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> of this document.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition.wr:WR1.__note"
A template for constraining the population of the entity data types defined in the <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> is described in annex E.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_context_association"
A **product_definition_context_association** is an association of a <<express:application_context_schema.product_definition_context,product_definition_context>> with a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>>, and specifies the meaning of this association.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_context_association.__example"
A <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>>, initially defined in the context of 'mechanical design', and in which the representation of the shape of a product is defined, may also be relevant in the context of 'process-planning design'. For such a case, the *product_definition_context_association* would relate the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> with the <<express:application_context_schema.product_definition_context,product_definition_context>> characterizing the context 'process-planning design' and the name of the role attribute would be 'other relevant context'.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_context_association.__note"
A *product_definition_context_association* may be used to associate a using context to a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>>. The defining context is associated to the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> using <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition.frame_of_reference,frame_of_reference>>.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_context_association.definition"
the reference to a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> associated to a context.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_context_association.frame_of_reference"
the <<express:application_context_schema.product_definition_context,product_definition_context>> that defines the stage in the product life cycle with which the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> is to be associated.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_context_association.role"
the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_context_role,product_definition_context_role>> that specifies the purpose of the association of the context of this **frame_of_reference** attribute with the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> of the **definition** attribute.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_context_association.role.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_context_role"
A **product_definition_context_role** is a specification of the purpose of a <<express:application_context_schema.product_definition_context,product_definition_context>>.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_context_role.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **product_definition_context_role** is known.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_context_role.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **product_definition_context_role**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_effectivity"
A **product_definition_effectivity** is a type of <<express:effectivity_schema.effectivity,effectivity>>. A **product_definition_effectivity** is the identification of a valid use of a particular <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> in the context of its participation in a given <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship,product_definition_relationship>>. The referenced <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> is the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> attribute of the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship,product_definition_relationship>>.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_effectivity.__note"
Appropriate subtypes of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship,product_definition_relationship>> and further information about the way to describe assemblies are specified in ISO 10303-44.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_effectivity.usage"
the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship,product_definition_relationship>> that defines the context of the <<express:effectivity_schema.effectivity,effectivity>>.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_effectivity.wr:WR1"
A **product_definition_effectivity** shall not be referred to as <<express:management_resources_schema.effectivity_assignment.assigned_effectivity,assigned_effectivity>>.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation"
A **product_definition_formation** is a collector of definitions of a product.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation.__example"
An application interpreted model could use this entity to support the identification of different versions of a single <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>>. Each version would be described by a group of instances of the entity data type <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> and each group, identified by a *product_definition_formation*, would be associated with the same <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>>.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **product_definition_formation**.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation.id.__example"
Part version number is an example of a *product_definition_formation* identifier.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation.id.__note"
The context in which id is used as a discriminating characteristic can be identified in an annotated Express schema that uses or specializes this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **product_definition_formation**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation.description.__note"
This attribute may be used to depict differences in the purpose and function of different formations of a single <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>>.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation.of_product"
the <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>> to which the **product_definition_formation** belongs.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation.of_product.__note"
A <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>> is associated with one or more *product_definition_formation* instances through the implicit inverse of this relationship.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation.ur:UR1"
The **id** of each **product_definition_formation** shall be unique within the collection of **product_definition_formations** that are related to the same product (through their attribute **of_product** {blank}).
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.final_solution"
A **final_solution** is a type of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation,product_definition_formation>> and is a set of additional sensual characteristics that can be applied to an occurrence that represents a neutral part in order to complete its definition.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.final_solution.status"
the text string that describes the level of completion between the neutral part and the final part.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.final_solution.specification"
the set of instances of the entity data type <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> that defines the various aspects of the **final_solution**.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation_relationship"
A **product_definition_formation_relationship** is a relationship between two instances of the entity data type <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation,product_definition_formation>> and provides an identification and description of this relationship.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation_relationship.__note"
A relationship may exist between instances of the entity data type <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation,product_definition_formation>> that relate to different instances of the entity data type <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>> or between different formations of the same <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>>.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation_relationship.__note"
The role of *product_definition_formation_relationship* can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation_relationship.__note"
Relationships represented using this entity may be parent child relationship. Annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity specify whether or not the relationship is directed.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation_relationship.__note"
This entity, together with the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation,product_definition_formation>> entity, is based on the relationship template that is described in annex E.3.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation_relationship.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **product_definition_formation_relationship**.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation_relationship.id.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation_relationship.id.__note"
The context in which id is used as a discriminating characteristic can be identified in an annotated Express schema that uses or specializes this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **product_definition_formation_relationship** is known.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **product_definition_formation_relationship**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation_relationship.relating_product_definition_formation"
one of the instances of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation,product_definition_formation>> that is a part of the relationship.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation_relationship.relating_product_definition_formation.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation_relationship.related_product_definition_formation"
the other instance of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation,product_definition_formation>> that is a part of the relationship. If one element of the relationship is dependent up on the other, this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation_relationship.related_product_definition_formation.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation_with_specified_source"
A **product_definition_formation_with_specified_source** is a type of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation,product_definition_formation>> whose source is identified to be either manufactured within an organization, bought, or the fact that this information is not known.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation_with_specified_source.make_or_buy"
the characterization of the source of the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation,product_definition_formation>>.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.generic_product_definition_reference"
A **generic_product_definition_reference** is a reference to an externally defined <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> that may or may not have a local representation. A **generic_product_definition_reference** is either a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_reference,product_definition_reference>> or a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_reference_with_local_representation,product_definition_reference_with_local_representation>>.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.generic_product_definition_reference.source"
defines the location which contains the original definition of the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>>.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_reference"
A **product_definition_reference** is a type of <<express:product_definition_schema.generic_product_definition_reference,generic_product_definition_reference>> that identifies the externally defined <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> by providing the key attributes necessary to unambiguously identify it and the associated <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation,product_definition_formation>>, <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>> and organization that owns the product id.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_reference.product_id"
specifies the identifier of the externally defined product, where the referenced <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> is assigned to one of its <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation,product_definition_formation>>.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_reference.product_definition_formation_id"
specifies the identifier of the externally defined <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_formation,product_definition_formation>>.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_reference.product_definition_id"
specifies the identifier of the externally defined <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>>.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_reference.id_owning_organization_name"
specifies the id owner of the externally defined product, realised by an applied <<express:management_resources_schema.organization_assignment,organization_assignment>> with the role 'id owner'.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_reference_with_local_representation"
A **product_definition_reference_with_local_representation** is a type of <<express:product_definition_schema.generic_product_definition_reference,generic_product_definition_reference>> that represents an externally defined <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> by a local <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>>.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship"
A **product_definition_relationship** is a relationship between two instances of the entity data type <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> or <<express:product_definition_schema.generic_product_definition_reference,generic_product_definition_reference>> and provides an identification and description of this relationship.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.__example"
The relationships within a bill-of-materials structure are examples of *product_definition_relationship* entity data types that associate different <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>>s. The relationship between a sketch and a detailed design is an example of a *product_definition_relationship* that associates different definitions of a single <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>>.
*)
(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.__example"
The same component could be used more than once in the same assembly. Each usage of the component would be specified as an instance of the *product_definition_relationship* entity.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.__note"
A relationship may exist between instances of the entity data type <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> that relate to different instances of the entity data type <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>> or between different definitions of the same <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>>.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.__note"
A single <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> may be used more than once within the description of a <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>>.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.__note"
The role of *product_definition_relationship* can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.__note"
Relationships represented using this entity may be parent child relationship. Annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity specify whether or not the relationship is directed.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.__note"
This entity, together with the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> entity, is based on the relationship template that is described in annex E.3.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **product_definition_relationship**.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.id.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.id.__note"
The context in which id is used as a discriminating characteristic can be identified in an annotated Express schema that uses or specializes this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **product_definition_relationship** is known.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **product_definition_relationship**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition"
one of the instances of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> that is a part of the relationship.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition.__note"
In the context of an ISO 10303 application protocol, the *product_definition_relationship* is an assembly component relationship, the *relating_product_definition* may be the assembly.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition"
the other instance of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> that is a part of the relationship. If one element of the relationship is dependent upon the other, this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition.__note"
In the context of an ISO 10303 application protocol, the *related_product_definition* may be the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> that is an element of the assembly.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship_relationship"
A **product_definition_relationship_relationship** is a relationship between two instances of the entity data type <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship,product_definition_relationship>> and provides an identification and description of this relationship.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship_relationship.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **product_definition_relationship_relationship**.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **product_definition_relationship_relationship** is known.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **product_definition_relationship_relationship**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship_relationship.relating"
one of the instances of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> that is a part of the relationship.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship_relationship.related"
the other instance of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> that is a part of the relationship. If one element of the relationship is dependent upon the other, this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_substitute"
A **product_definition_substitute** is an association of a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> with a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship,product_definition_relationship>>. The association states the fact that the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> may replace, in the context of the relationship, the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> that is specified in the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> attribute of the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship,product_definition_relationship>>.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_substitute.__example"
Two kinds of ball-point pens may be manufactured: a standard model and a deluxe model. Each model of the pen would be specified as a separate <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> related to a particular kind of nib: a standard nib and a deluxe nib, respectively. The fact that the deluxe nib and the standard nib are interchangeable only in the context of the standard model of ball-point pen is established with this construct.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_substitute.__note"
If a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship,product_definition_relationship>> exists between a component part and its assembly, a *product_definition_substitute* could be used to capture an allowable substitute, that is, a different component part that may be used as a replacement in the same assembly.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_substitute.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **product_definition_substitute**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_substitute.context_relationship"
the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship,product_definition_relationship>> that specifies the context in which the replacement may occur.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_substitute.context_relationship.__example"
In the previous example, the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.relating_product_definition,relating_product_definition>> of a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship,product_definition_relationship>> identified as a *context_relationship* would be the standard model of the ball-point pen and the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> would be the standard nib.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_substitute.substitute_definition"
the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> that acts as an allowed replacement for the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition_relationship.related_product_definition,related_product_definition>> of the **context_relationship**.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_substitute.substitute_definition.__example"
In the previous example, this attribute would identify the deluxe nib .
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_substitute.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **product_definition_substitute** is known.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_substitute.name.__note"
This attribute is an upwardly compatible addition to <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> as specified in ISO 10303-41:1994.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_substitute.wr:WR1"
A <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> shall not be defined as a substitute for itself.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_substitute.wr:WR2"
Each **product_definition_substitute** shall be the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute.named_item,named_item>> in at most one <<express:basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute,name_attribute>>.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_substitute.wr:WR2.__note"
The <<express:basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute,name_attribute>> data type is defined in <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> of this document
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_substitute.wr:WR2.__note"
A template for constraining the population of the entity data types defined in the <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> is described in annex E.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_with_associated_documents"
A **product_definition_with_associated_documents** is a type of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> in which the associated documents participate in the definition of the product.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_definition_with_associated_documents.documentation_ids"
the set of instances of <<express:document_schema.document,document>> entity data type that are associated with the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>>.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_related_product_category"
A **product_related_product_category** is a type of <<express:product_definition_schema.product_category,product_category>> that identifies products that satisfy the type identified by the category.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_related_product_category.products"
a set of <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>>s that belong to the **product_related_product_category**.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_relationship"
A **product_relationship** is a relationship between two instances of the entity data type <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>> and provides an identification and description of their relationship.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_relationship.__note"
The role of *product_relationship* can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_relationship.__note"
Relationships represented using this entity may be parent child relationship. Annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity specify whether or not the relationship is directed.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_relationship.__note"
This entity, together with the <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>> entity, is based on the relationship template that is described in annex E.3.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_relationship.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **product_relationship**.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_relationship.id.__note"
The context in which id is used as a discriminating characteristic can be identified in an annotated Express schema that uses or specializes this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **product_relationship** is known.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **product_relationship**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_relationship.relating_product"
one of the instances of <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>> that is a part of the relationship.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_relationship.relating_product.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.product_relationship.related_product"
the other instance of <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>> that is a part of the relationship. If one element of the relationship is dependent up on the other, this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.product_relationship.related_product.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.acyclic_product_category_relationship"
The **acyclic_product_category_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:product_definition_schema.product_category,product_category>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_category_relationship,product_category_relationship>> or any of its subtypes. The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.acyclic_product_category_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.
*)

(*"product_definition_schema.acyclic_product_category_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate <<express:product_definition_schema.product_category_relationship,product_category_relationship>> to be checked.
*)


(*"product_definition_schema.acyclic_product_category_relationship.children"
(input) the set of instances of the entity data type <<express:product_definition_schema.product_category,product_category>> that the function is searching for in the category field of the **relation** argument.
*)


